--TEST--
A socket opens a `wss` URL and reports the subprotocol the handshake settled on, and a peer choosing a name that was never offered is refused — `rule:http-server/an-outbound-socket-is-opened-like-an-outbound-call`, `rule:http-server/allow-url-pins-the-address`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Http\Socket::protocol
// The secure half of the roster, opened the way every outbound call is: the URL
// goes through the row that speaks `ws` and `wss`, and the bag carries what this
// end offered. `protocol()` reads back the one name both ends agreed on.
Core\Test::answerSocket("wss://gateway.example.com/v1", ["ready"], {protocol: "chat.v2"});

var $socket = Core\Http\Client::openSocket("wss://gateway.example.com/v1", {
    protocols: ["chat.v1", "chat.v2"],
});
echo "protocol=", $socket->protocol() ?? "none", "\n";
echo "first ", $socket->receive()?->text() ?? "-", "\n";

// A peer that chooses a name nobody offered is answering a question nobody
// asked, and a program reading `protocol()` afterwards would act on it — so the
// handshake is refused instead of completing.
Core\Test::answerSocket("wss://gateway.example.com/v2", ["ready"], {protocol: "chat.v9"});
try {
    var $stray = Core\Http\Client::openSocket("wss://gateway.example.com/v2", {
        protocols: ["chat.v1"],
    });
} catch (RuntimeError $unoffered) {
    echo $unoffered->message, "\n";
}

// A call that offered nothing settles on nothing, which is the same reading one
// step earlier: a name is chosen only out of the ones that were on the table.
Core\Test::answerSocket("wss://gateway.example.com/v3", ["ready"]);
var $bare = Core\Http\Client::openSocket("wss://gateway.example.com/v3");
echo "bare=", $bare->protocol() ?? "none", "\n";

// Nothing left this process: the socket that opened is the table's, and the one
// that was refused sent no frame before it threw.
echo "sent=", Core\Arr::count(Core\Test::sentSocket()), "\n";
--EXPECT--
protocol=chat.v2
first ready
Core\Http\Client::openSocket: the peer chose the subprotocol `chat.v9`, which this call never offered
bare=none
sent=0
